The "main.cpp" is a generic main driver which can link with any of
the sort (and potentially other) functions. It expects to call a
function that has the signature:

         extern int Function(int *A, int size, int verbose);

where <A> is an array of integers of length <size>, and <verbose>
is a flag that says wether we want detailed printouts.

main.cpp has the following options:

    -l          do one run and print the ids
    -n <N>	set the size of the array [100]
    -m <M>	set the number of monte-carlo trials [1]
    -p <i,P>	probability of a fault at the specified id [0.0]
    -s <S>	specify random integer seed [use time()]
    -v		be quite verbose [no, be quiet]
    -h		print this help

so the basic usage is to make one of the sort programs, run it with
the -l option to get the location ides, and then run it with the -m
and -p options to inject errors.

step 1: making:

SDConLLM/adad$ make selection
g++ -O3 -flto   -c -o selection.o selection.cpp
g++ -O3 -flto   -c -o hash.o hash.cpp
g++ -O3 -flto   -c -o adad.o adad.cpp
g++ -O3 -flto   -c -o fault.o fault.cpp
g++ -O3 -flto   -c -o main.o main.cpp
g++ -O3 -flto -o selection selection.o hash.o adad.o fault.o main.o

step 2: listing the fault locations

SDConLLM/adad$ ./selection -l
SEED=839109 
Fault Locations:
	id	description
	7	A!=A2   selection                           0x0000000107222d9a main + 714
	6	A+=K2   selection                           0x0000000107222d9a main + 714
	3	A<A2   selection                           0x0000000107222d9a main + 714
	5	A=A+K2   selection                           0x0000000107222d9a main + 714
	2	A=A-K2   selection                           0x0000000107222d9a main + 714
	4	A=A2   selection                           0x0000000107222d9a main + 714
	1	A=K2   selection                           0x0000000107222d9a main + 714

id is the fault id, the description shows:
    the operator (e.g. A=A+K)
    the name of the function in which that operator is
    the offset of that operator in the binary program

note: there is an extra "2" after the operator which should be ignored
otherwise the operator has "A" for a adad, "K" for a constanct, and
the usual operators otherwise

step 3: run the code:

SDConLLM/adad$ ./selection -m 20 -p 3,1
SEED=503695 
./selection 
	size	100	trials	20
	sdc	20	core	0
Injection Fault_Probs:
	id	prob
	3	1
Fault Counts:
	3	20

the above ran 20 calls, injecting errors at id #3 with 100% probability
and it produced 20 sdc, and 0 core dumps

The core dumps are flagged when the code tries to access the array outside
its bounds
